---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Mermaid from '../components/Mermaid.astro';
import { withBase } from '../utils/url';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="Learning paths"
			description="Suggested routes through Linux internals — boot, processes, memory, VFS, networking, sync, containers, and more."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<header class="page-head animate-rise">
				<h1>Learning paths</h1>
				<p>
					Pick a trail. Each path points at notes on this site and classic open sources so you can
					learn without paying for a course.
				</p>
			</header>

			<section class="overview diagram">
				<h2>The curriculum map</h2>
				<script type="text/plain" class="mermaid-source">
mindmap
  root((Paths))
    A Boot
    B Process
    C Memory syscalls
    D VFS
    E Networking
    F Sync drivers
    G Containers
				</script>
			</section>

			<section class="path animate-rise-delay">
				<h2>Path A — From power-on to PID 1</h2>
				<p>Follow the machine from firmware into the kernel and the first userspace process.</p>
				<script type="text/plain" class="mermaid-source">
timeline
  title Path A — boot
  Firmware : UEFI / BIOS
  Bootloader : GRUB / systemd-boot
  Kernel setup : decompress + setup_arch
  start_kernel : init/main.c
  Userspace : init / systemd
				</script>
				<ul>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/how-the-kernel-boots')}>How the kernel boots</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/procfs-and-observability')}>procfs and observability</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/bpf-and-tracing-intro')}>BPF and tracing intro</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/reading-an-oops')}>Reading an oops</a></li>
					<li>
						External: <a href="https://docs.kernel.org/admin-guide/init.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
							>kernel.org — init</a
						>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section class="path">
				<h2>Path B — Process &amp; scheduler</h2>
				<p>What is a task_struct, how does fork work, and who runs next?</p>
				<script type="text/plain" class="mermaid-source">
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> Running
  Running --> Sleeping: block
  Sleeping --> Running: wake
  Running --> Runnable: preempt
  Runnable --> Running: pick_next
  Running --> Zombie: exit
  Zombie --> [*]: wait
				</script>
				<ul>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/anatomy-of-a-linux-process')}>Anatomy of a Linux process</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/signals-and-process-lifecycle')}>Signals and process lifecycle</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/scheduler-cfs-and-eevdf')}>Scheduler: CFS and EEVDF</a></li>
					<li>
						External: <a href="https://docs.kernel.org/scheduler/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
							>kernel.org — scheduler</a
						>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section class="path">
				<h2>Path C — Memory &amp; syscalls</h2>
				<p>Cross the userspace/kernel boundary, then walk virtual memory.</p>
				<script type="text/plain" class="mermaid-source">
sequenceDiagram
  participant App
  participant libc
  participant Kernel
  App->>libc: open(...)
  libc->>Kernel: syscall
  Kernel-->>libc: fd / errno
  libc-->>App: return
				</script>
				<ul>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/syscalls-crossing-the-boundary')}>Syscalls: crossing the boundary</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/vdso-and-vsyscall')}>vDSO and vsyscall</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/virtual-memory-walkthrough')}>Virtual memory walkthrough</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/page-tables-and-tlb')}>Page tables and the TLB</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/page-cache-and-writeback')}>Page cache and writeback</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/slab-allocator-and-kmalloc')}>Slab allocator and kmalloc</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/mmap-and-page-faults-deep')}>mmap and page faults (deep)</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/userfaultfd-and-remote-faults')}>userfaultfd and remote faults</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/epoll-and-event-loops')}>epoll and event loops</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/memory-reclaim-and-oom')}>Memory reclaim and OOM</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/timers-and-timekeeping')}>Timers and timekeeping</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/elf-loading-and-dynamic-linking')}>ELF loading and dynamic linking</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/reading-kernel-source')}>Reading kernel source: where to start</a></li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section class="path">
				<h2>Path D — Filesystems &amp; VFS</h2>
				<p>Pathnames become dentries, inodes, and file objects.</p>
				<script type="text/plain" class="mermaid-source">
classDiagram
  class dentry {
    +d_name
    +d_inode
  }
  class inode {
    +i_mode
    +i_mapping
  }
  class file {
    +f_pos
    +f_op
  }
  dentry --> inode : points to
  file --> inode : opens
  file --> file_operations : f_op
  class file_operations {
    +read()
    +write()
  }
				</script>
				<ul>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/vfs-and-the-open-path')}>VFS and the open path</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/walking-openat-in-the-source')}>Source walk: openat</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/block-layer-and-bio')}>Block layer and bio</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/ext4-on-disk-sketch')}>ext4 on-disk sketch</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/io-uring-intro')}>io_uring intro</a></li>
					<li>
						External: <a href="https://docs.kernel.org/filesystems/vfs.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
							>kernel.org — VFS</a
						>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section class="path">
				<h2>Path E — Networking</h2>
				<p>Sockets, sk_buff, and how packets climb the stack.</p>
				<script type="text/plain" class="mermaid-source">
sequenceDiagram
  participant App
  participant TCP
  participant IP
  participant NIC
  App->>TCP: sendmsg
  TCP->>IP: sk_buff
  IP->>NIC: xmit
  NIC-->>IP: RX skb
  IP-->>TCP: deliver
  TCP-->>App: recvmsg
				</script>
				<ul>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/sockets-and-the-networking-stack')}>Sockets and the networking stack</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/af-unix-sockets')}>AF_UNIX sockets</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/tcp-state-machine-sketch')}>TCP state machine sketch</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/napi-and-softnet')}>NAPI and softnet</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/netfilter-and-hooks-sketch')}>Netfilter hooks sketch</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/epoll-and-event-loops')}>epoll and event loops</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/interrupts-softirqs-and-tasklets')}>Interrupts and softirqs</a></li>
					<li>
						External: <a href="https://docs.kernel.org/networking/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
							>kernel.org — networking</a
						>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section class="path">
				<h2>Path F — Concurrency &amp; drivers</h2>
				<p>Locks, RCU, modules, and the device model.</p>
				<script type="text/plain" class="mermaid-source">
sequenceDiagram
  participant HW as Device
  participant Top as Hard IRQ
  participant Soft as Softirq
  participant Drv as Driver / locks
  HW->>Top: IRQ
  Top->>Soft: schedule bottom half
  Soft->>Drv: process + sync
				</script>
				<ul>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/locks-spinlocks-mutexes-rcu')}>Locks: spinlocks, mutexes, RCU</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/rcu-grace-periods')}>RCU grace periods</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/futexes-userspace-to-kernel')}>Futexes: userspace to kernel</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/workqueues-and-kthreads')}>Workqueues and kthreads</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/kernel-modules-and-device-model')}>Kernel modules and the device model</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/interrupts-softirqs-and-tasklets')}>Interrupts, softirqs, and bottom halves</a></li>
				</ul>
			</section>

			<section class="path">
				<h2>Path G — Containers</h2>
				<p>Namespaces isolate views; cgroups enforce limits.</p>
				<script type="text/plain" class="mermaid-source">
mindmap
  root((Container))
    Namespaces
      pid
      net
      mnt
      user
    cgroups
      cpu
      memory
      io
				</script>
				<ul>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/namespaces-and-cgroups')}>Namespaces and cgroups</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/pid-namespaces-deep')}>PID namespaces (deep)</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/mount-namespaces-and-bind-mounts')}>Mount namespaces and bind mounts</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/cgroup-v2-controllers')}>cgroup v2 controllers</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/capabilities-and-lsm-intro')}>Capabilities and LSM intro</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/seccomp-bpf-intro')}>seccomp-BPF intro</a></li>
					<li><a href={withBase('blog/anatomy-of-a-linux-process')}>Anatomy of a Linux process</a></li>
					<li>
						External:
						<a href="https://docs.kernel.org/admin-guide/cgroup-v2.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
							>cgroup v2</a
						>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
		<Mermaid />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	main {
		width: var(--max);
		max-width: calc(100% - 2em);
	}
	.page-head p {
		color: var(--ink-muted);
	}
	.overview {
		margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;
		padding: 1.5rem;
		background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85);
		border: 1px solid var(--line);
		border-radius: var(--radius);
		box-shadow: var(--shadow);
	}
	.overview h2 {
		margin-top: 0;
	}
	.path {
		margin: 2.5rem 0;
		padding: 1.5rem;
		background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8);
		border: 1px solid var(--line);
		border-radius: var(--radius);
	}
	.path h2 {
		margin-top: 0;
	}
	.path p {
		color: var(--ink-muted);
	}
</style>
